"""Session 12. Your data roadmap and 90-day plan. A PRACTICAL session and the close of the course (rebuild of 4 November 2026).

The learner turns the Session 4 assessment (inventory, scorecard, top three gaps) into a data roadmap with phases, owners, dates, effort, dependencies and success measures,
plans what to test first (retrieval before training, from Session 0), sets the 30, 60 and 90 day check-ins and shares the roadmap in pairs (no presentations, no demo day).
Column names on the slides match the 90-Day Roadmap template as it is being updated elsewhere (4 Nov 2026): Phase, Action, Owner, Start, Due, Effort (hours), Depends on, Success measure, Status.
Phase values used here: Protect and clean (days 1 to 30), Describe and prepare (days 31 to 60), Test and decide (days 61 to 90); the template must carry the same three names.
Follow-up Kit/ (30-60-90 Check-in Form.docx, Results Tracker.xlsx, Sponsor Briefing.docx) are updated by someone else.
The NVF example plan starts on 1 February 2027: day 30 is 3 March 2027, day 60 is 2 April 2027, day 90 is 2 May 2027. The NVF roadmap lines (owners, hours, targets) are
invented teaching values, labelled as estimates. No AI result is shown in this session.
"""

